Back Online Today: the LetsFixWP brand film (45 s), in the Tabletop App Flythrough style

Code: src/film.js, src/shots.js, audio/*.py, index.html and build.sh were written for this film. The engine files
src/world.js, cards.js, voxel.js, anim.js, camera.js, post.js, main.js, captions.js and tools/camspeed.mjs come from the
Lemo-Opuscar library's Tabletop App Flythrough demo (MIT, Lemomo / LemoLab, github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar).
The renderer, reading-time check, TTS and speech-check wrappers, sampler and foley helpers are the library's core/ (MIT).
three.js r170 (MIT), loaded from the library's node_modules.

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1; licence texts in fonts/; downloaded by build.sh from github.com/google/fonts):
  Manrope (fonts/Manrope.ttf), JetBrains Mono (fonts/JetBrainsMono.ttf).

Voice-over: Microsoft neural text-to-speech, voice en-IN-NeerjaNeural, through edge-tts (the free Edge "Read aloud" service).
  This service's terms do not clearly grant commercial use. Before the film runs in paid ads, either re-voice the same
  lines with the same voice on a paid Azure AI Speech subscription (commercial use licensed), or record a person.
  The lines are in vo/lines.json; build.sh rebuilds everything else around a new recording.
Speech check: faster-whisper, model small.en (MIT); used to verify the voice, not part of the film.

Music samples (CC0 1.0, no attribution required; acknowledged): VS Chamber Orchestra: Community Edition (Versilian Studios),
  Versilian Community Sample Library (Versilian Studios). Instruments: marimba, vibraphone, glockenspiel, contrabass,
  contrabass pizz, cellos, cellos pizz, violas, horn, timpani, suspended cymbal, claps, shaker.
Kick drum, room tone and all foley: synthesised in code (audio/compose.py, audio/foley.py, the library's core/audio/sfx.py).

Pixel art (Pip the site, the three developers, the visitors, the key, the envelope), the browser, phone, price, access and team
cards, the backup tower, the desk props, wood and paper textures: drawn in code. No photographs, no generated images,
no third-party logos. "your-site" and the shop on the browser card are fictional.

Facts on screen and in the voice: the owner-confirmed promises in PRODUCT.md (fixed price agreed before work starts,
a full backup before any change, a login the client creates and never their password, access removed when done)
and the home page H1 "Back online today". No prices, counts, ratings or turnaround figures.
